<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 11 trln rbls bills Sept 25.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 11 trln rbls bills Sept 25.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian finance ministry will auction four trillion roubles of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills and seven trillion roubles of six-month bills on September 25, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Details of the three-month T-bills:</p>
<p>    Series number			    21071</p>
<p>    Issue volume			     4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor					119 days</p>
<p>    Issue date				 Sept 25, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date			    Jan 22, 1997</p>
<p>The bills run for four months but are officially classified as three-month paper.</p>
<p>Details of the six-month T-bills:</p>
<p>    Series number			    22051</p>
<p>    Issue volume			     7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor					238 days</p>
<p>    Issue date				 Sept 25, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date			    May 21, 1997</p>
<p>The bills run for eight months, but are officially classified as six-month paper.</p>
<p>On September 25 the finance ministry will also repay about 7.25 trillion roubles in maturing six-month bills (series 22033).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
